  "id": "true-experiment",
  "term": "true experiment",
  "definition": "A true experiment is a research design that tests an effect by comparing an experimental condition with a control condition and assigning participants by randomization. Its aim is to isolate whether differences between groups are due to the manipulated condition rather than other factors.",
